        "page": 4,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p4_s11"
      },
      "text": "Host: bee.businessconsults.net As early as March 2011, Joe Stewart at Dell SecureWorks reported that various subdomains off the primary domain of \"businessconsults.net\" have acted as command and control nodes for the well­known \"HUC Packet Transmit Tool\" (aka \"HTran\") [2] , which is a light­weight TCP proxy tool used by the nation state threat actor that breached RSA around that time, labeled by",
